<title>NORWAY: Conoco spuds dry well near N.Sea Balder field.</title>
<headline>Conoco spuds dry well near N.Sea Balder field.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norske Conoco, as operator of licence 103, has completed drilling of exploration well 25/7-4 northwest of the North Sea Balder field, the Norwegian Oil Directorate (OD) said on Monday.</p>
<p>No hydrocarbons were discovered at the well, which was permanently plugged, the OD said.</p>
<p>Dupont unit Conoco holds 37.5 percent of licence 103 and is partnered by Den norske stats oljeselskap AS with a 50 percent stake and Amerada Hess with 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
